diff --git a/docs/src/platform-support.md b/docs/src/platform-support.md
index cb4f504..163f875 100644
--- a/docs/src/platform-support.md
+++ b/docs/src/platform-support.md
@@ -83,4 +83,21 @@ with a synthetic address. Compilation and validation do not prove runtime safety
-This experimental support does not yet provide a physical-memory access API.
-Pointer arithmetic and comparisons, aggregate pointer storage, atomics and
-reference validity need separate lowering and evidence. Do not infer those
-guarantees from a valid conversion. Formatted u32 panic arguments are tested
+Physical pointer equality and inequality compare 64-bit addresses because
+SPIR-V's pointer comparison instructions exclude PhysicalStorageBuffer.
+Existing logical pointer legalization runs first for offsets. The remaining
+sized raw-pointer case uses pointer-width byte arithmetic with the pointee's
+stride, preserving wrapping behavior. Storage inference still rejects integer
+address conversions from logical storage classes.
+
+The current operation evidence is deliberately narrower than `*mut` parity:
+
+| Operation | Observed compiler boundary |
+| --- | --- |
+| `==`, `!=`, `<` on typed physical u32 pointers | 64-bit address comparisons compile and validate |
+| `wrapping_add`, `wrapping_sub`, `wrapping_offset` | u32-pointer fixtures retain full-width stride arithmetic, including a negative offset with rustc optimization enabled |
+| `core::ptr::null_mut`, u32-pointer `is_null` | diagnosed as unsupported typed-pointer casts inside these standard-library helpers |
+| logical pointer address comparison on physical64 | rejected after storage-class inference |
+| other pointer casts, aggregate accesses, volatile intrinsics, copies, atomics, references and allocation-dependent methods | require separate lowering, diagnostics and execution evidence |
+
+These tests transport addresses without dereferencing them. They do not prove
+GPU behavior or the allocation, aliasing and lifetime obligations of in-bounds
+methods. This experimental support does not yet provide a physical-memory
+access API. Formatted u32 panic arguments are tested
diff --git a/tests/compiletests/ui/physical_storage/pointer_compare_physical64.rs b/tests/compiletests/ui/physical_storage/pointer_compare_physical64.rs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f60faf6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/compiletests/ui/physical_storage/pointer_compare_physical64.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+// build-pass
+// only-vulkan1.3_physical64
+// compile-flags: -C llvm-args=--disassemble
+// normalize-stderr-test "\n\W*OpSource .*" -> ""
+// normalize-stderr-test "\n\W*OpLine .*" -> ""
+// normalize-stderr-test "\n\W*%\d+ = OpString .*" -> ""
+
+#![forbid(unsafe_code)]
+
+use spirv_std::spirv;
+
+#[spirv(compute(threads(1)))]
+pub fn main(
+    #[spirv(push_constant)] addresses: &[u64; 2],
+    #[spirv(storage_buffer, descriptor_set = 0, binding = 0)] output: &mut [u32; 3],
+) {
+    // Comparisons transport address information only. No pointer is dereferenced.
+    let left = addresses[0] as *mut u32;
+    let right = addresses[1] as *mut u32;
+    output[0] = (left == right) as u32;
+    output[1] = (left != right) as u32;
+    output[2] = (left < right) as u32;
+}
